# UI design (mandatory)

Read `docs-site/content/ui-design-principles.md` before building or changing screens.

## Must

- Use `src/shared/theme/tokens.ts` — no random hex in feature styles
- Wrap screens in `Screen`; actions via `Button` (primary/secondary/ghost)
- One primary CTA per screen (accent `Button`)
- Padding: `spacing.lg` horizontal; min tap height 48pt
- Handle loading (spinner/disabled), error (inline text), empty (CTA)

## Components

Add reusable UI only to `src/shared/ui/`. Feature screens compose — don't copy-paste card/button styles.

## Mobile vs web

- Mobile product: `src/features/*/ui/`
- Recipient web: same tokens, max-width ~480px — not in docs-site product flows
- docs-site: docs shell only

## Don't

- Invent new color palette or generic purple AI aesthetic
- Raw `TextInput` without plan to move to shared `Input`
- Full-screen blocking loader for quick ops
- Multiple competing primary buttons on one screen
